    "comment": "The contract. Every consumer decodes each frames vector with its production decoder and validates each controlFrame instance against #/$defs/controlFrame, then asserts the verdict. Three JSON parsers and three regex engines are in play, so agreement here is worth more than the schema text.",
    "schema": "control.schema.json",
    "notes": [
        "frames: hex is the whole websocket message, magic included.",
        "canonical: true means every encoder reproduces hex byte for byte from arm and fields.",
        "Reasons are printable ASCII by schema, so every valid error frame has one canonical encoding and every encoder writes those bytes for it; only \" and \\ are ever escaped.",
        "The JSON after the magic of every valid frame, and of every invalid frame whose why starts with law 3, must also agree with the schema.",
        "Law 1 and law 2 failures are not schema cases: the decoder rejects them before validation. why starts with the law at which every consumer rejects the vector; a vector on which the consumers stop at different laws stays out of this file (an integer token of 1001 digits or more, keys that are distinct lone-surrogate escapes).",
        "Numbers are integer tokens: a fraction or exponent fails law 2 even where the schema would accept the value as an integer.",
        "MAX_CONTROL_FRAME_BYTES is 32768: the largest canonical frame is 8222 bytes (an error whose 4096-character reason is all escaped quotes or backslashes); a peer that escapes every reason character as \\u00XX writes 24606, and JSON whitespace may pad any valid frame up to the bound. Boundary recipe every decoder test pins with literals: the ping vector followed by spaces to exactly 32768 bytes decodes; 32769 bytes fails law 2.",
        "canonical: false marks a valid vector no conforming encoder writes (whitespace around or between tokens, members in another order); every decoder must still accept it and yield arm and fields.",
        "A law-2 vector is shaped so that a lenient parser (last key wins, encoding sniffed, fractions kept) turns it into a schema-valid frame; the verdict alone then catches a decoder that skipped the rule.",
        "String bounds count Unicode code points in every engine; every case that tests a bound is ASCII, where code points, UTF-16 units and bytes coincide.",
        "Every keyword of control.schema.json is pinned by a case that fails only through it, or is redundant by construction: sessionUuid minLength sits behind the fixed-width pattern and errorReason type behind not/pattern."
    ],
